What Exactly Is a Generative Engine?
Generative engines are AI systems capable of producing original responses by synthesizing information from the web, databases, and pre-trained models. These include:

ChatGPT (OpenAI)

Google SGE (Search Generative Experience)

Claude (Anthropic)

Perplexity AI

Microsoft Copilot

Meta AI

Amazon’s Rufus (for product queries)

They don’t just index—they understand, rephrase, combine, and generate. So, unlike traditional search engines, they don’t give users 10 blue links. They give direct answers, backed by trusted content.

This is where Generative Engine Optimization comes in.

